  journal   = "Journal of clinical virology: the official publication of the Pan
               American Society for Clinical Virology",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  abstract  = "Yellow fever, a mosquito-borne flavivirus disease occurs in
               tropical areas of South America and Africa. It is a disease of
               major historical importance, but remains a threat to travelers to
               and residents of endemic areas despite the availability of an
               effective vaccine for nearly 70 years. An important aspect is the
               receptivity of many non-endemic areas to introduction and spread
               of yellow fever. This paper reviews the clinical aspects,
               pathogenesis, and epidemiology of yellow fever, with an emphasis
               on recent changes in the distribution and incidence of the
               disease. Recent knowledge about yellow fever 17D vaccine
               mechanism of action and safety are discussed.",
  year      =  2015
}

